dcomp: cross-process shared visuals, window surfaces and a scale transform, so WebView2 pages
hosted through a composition visual (Clip Studio Paint 5.1.5's sign-up panel and welcome dialog)
are drawn.

Applies to Wine 11.20 with wine-staging 11.20's dcomp-DCompositionCreateDevice2 patch set applied
(patches/dcomp-DCompositionCreateDevice2/00*.patch, patch -p1). Build dlls/dcomp/x86_64-windows/dcomp.dll
as for d2d1-source-copy.patch, strip it, and install it as the runner's dcomp.dll.

- IDCompositionDesktopDevicePartner::CreateSharedResource / OpenSharedResourceHandle and
  DCompositionCreateSharedVisualHandle: the handle is a section, so it survives DuplicateHandle into
  the browser process; no wineserver change. The target created from it renders its tree into a
  named section and the visual created from it blends that into the host's window (shared.c).
- CreateSurfaceFromHwnd: a surface standing for what this process' targets compose into that window
  (needs --in-process-gpu); those targets are no longer drawn on screen.
- CreateScaleTransform, SetTransformObject, SetClip return success; SetOffsetY and the translation
  of SetTransform are applied.

